{"author":"Joe Oakhart","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"74949af2c237e0661f29c0207e9255003fed6d859800f5c041dadc4d500482cc","digest":{"component_or_area":"store write lock management","key_entities":["src/rebar/_store/lock.py","src/rebar/_store/lock_owner.py","_mkdir_lock_is_stale","_process_start_time","_pid_alive","_mkdir_lock_age_exceeds_ceiling","_MKDIR_LOCK_STALE_CEILING_S","_reclaim_mkdir_lock","_owner_stamp","tests/unit/test_lock_age_ceiling.py"],"problem_keywords":["stale lock","pid recycling","process start time","/proc unavailable","macOS","unbounded wedge","lock holder reclamation"],"propositions":["On platforms without /proc (macOS), _process_start_time returns None, making the recycled-pid discriminator unsatisfiable and causing dead processes with recycled pids to be treated as live indefinitely","When a live-pid verdict is unqualified (current_start is None), the lock should be reclaimed if it exceeds the 1-hour ceiling, not held unboundedly","The dual-leg invariant ensures that a genuinely live, non-recycled owner cannot reach the stale check, so the ceiling can only fire on orphan cases without breaking live owners","The owner-identity and staleness cluster was extracted from lock.py (798 LOC) into lock_owner.py to respect the 800-LOC module size limit"]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1787537212138554001,"uuid":"b25e7ee2-52e7-4a4d-be5e-9f2d7dd70940"}